=== layout: section

# Chapter 13: Synthetic biology and fuels

=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 14: Starch fuel

@body

- The basic idea is familiar: turn starch into sugar, then let yeast make alcohol.
- Amylases help break down starch. Glucoamylase releases glucose for fermentation.
- Yeast converts sugar into ethanol and carbon dioxide. Distillation and drying concentrate the fuel.
- The biological reaction works. Is growing food to feed a fuel tank a good use of land?

@notes

