=== layout: one-panel

# 14. Why Alcohol?

@body

- Good\:
  - Can be synthesized biologically or chemically
  - High octane can support efficient engine designs
- Bad\:
  - lower energy density = less energy per gallon
    - ethanol is oxidized form of ethane
- Typically produced from biomass (sugars) through fermentation

@notes

Source: ../old/lect06c-set_4_TP-chapter_12-16_material.odp, slide 16.
2026 topic 14: starch fuel. Original content retained and regrouped.

