=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 15: Cellulose fuel

@body

- Why use the corn kernel if we could use the stalk?
- Cellulose packs glucose into strong fibers. Hemicellulose and lignin add more obstacles in plant cell walls.
- Pretreatment exposes the material; cellulases and beta-glucosidases help release sugars.
- Getting sugar out cheaply is a different problem from fermenting sugar into ethanol.

@notes

2026 topic 15; numbering authority: ../old/2026_topic_list.txt.
