=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 16: Biodiesel

@body

- Used cooking oil contains useful energy. It is not automatically ready for a diesel engine.
- [*Transesterification*]{underline=true} exchanges the alcohol component of an ester.
- Triglyceride plus methanol produces *fatty acid methyl esters (FAME)* and glycerol.
- FAME biodiesel contains ester groups. Petroleum diesel is mostly hydrocarbons.

@notes

2026 topic 16; numbering authority: ../old/2026_topic_list.txt.
Prompt source: ../old/Fall_2026_Talking_Points_Set_4-Environmental_and_Synthetic.pptx, slide 46.
