=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 17: Algae diesel

@body

- Pond scum fuel. It sounds great: sunlight, carbon dioxide, and a lot of little oil-producing cells.
- Algae can store carbon in lipids, but rapid growth and high oil content do not always peak together.
- Harvesting cells from lots of water can consume a lot of energy.
- Follow the process all the way to usable fuel before calling it cheap or sustainable.

@notes

2026 topic 17; numbering authority: ../old/2026_topic_list.txt.
