=== layout: one-panel

# 17. Types of Biofuels

@body

- *Bio-alcohols* – biologically produced alcohols, most commonly ethanol
- *Bio-diesel* – produced from oils or fats – similar in composition to fossil diesel.
- *Algae fuel* – CO2 and sunlight to produce either ethanol or hydrocarbons.
- *Cellulosic fuels* – cellulose-based fuel – stalks of wheat, corn, and wood converted to ethanol

@notes

Source: ../old/lect06c-set_4_TP-chapter_12-16_material.odp, slide 52.
2026 topic 17: algae diesel. Original content retained and regrouped.

=== layout: two-panels

# 17. Two routes from algae to fuel

@left

## Extract the oil

- Harvest cells and recover lipids.
- Convert suitable oils to FAME.
- Compare cell disruption and purification costs.

@right

## Process the wet biomass

- Hydrothermal liquefaction makes biocrude.
- Further upgrading makes usable fuels.
- Biocrude and FAME are chemically different products.

@notes

