# 18. A helix is not yet a genetic system

@body

- Draw a natural base pair next to an xDNA pair. Where is the added benzene ring?
- For a particular XNA, can it pair with itself, DNA, or RNA? Do not assume every chemistry behaves the same way.
- How can engineered polymerases move information between DNA and XNA? What would demonstrate heredity and evolution?
- Compare proposed uses in aptamers, stable probes, and data storage. What do we know about toxicity, delivery, copying accuracy, and cost?

@notes

