# 19. When would you call it alive?

@body

- Compare lipid vesicles, coacervates, and polymer compartments. What function does each construction actually demonstrate?
- Can the system reproduce repeatedly, maintain itself, and evolve? Which of those criteria are missing?
- Why build an artificial organelle inside a cell rather than build an entire cell?
- What can these experiments teach us about the origin of life? Would you recognize life elsewhere if its chemistry differed from ours?

@notes

