# Topic 20: Synthetic chloroplasts

@body

- Plants already do photosynthesis. Why try to rebuild part of it?
- One goal is to combine light-powered energy production with a redesigned carbon-fixation pathway.
- A 2020 chloroplast mimic coupled thylakoid membranes to a synthetic CO2-fixation cycle in droplets.
- That is a working biochemical system. It is not a complete, self-reproducing chloroplast.

@notes

