# Topic 21: Minimal genome

@body

- How many genes does a cell need? First ask: living where, on what food?
- A minimal genome is minimal under specified conditions. A rich laboratory medium supplies things the cell no longer makes.
- JCVI-syn1.0 used a chemically synthesized genome transplanted into a recipient cell.
- The genome was synthetic; the starting cellular machinery was inherited from a living cell.

@notes

